ngs that are  pushing up prices that are putting so  many pressures on people and that could  that could involve  a cancelling the national insurance rise  cutting  business rates for small businesses you  know finding ways to get pockets to get  money into people's pockets and and to  tackle inflation we need that now what  we've got at the moment is just this  kind of slow drift from the government  and hope that things will get better  so i think i picked up there you said  you might cancel the national insurance  right is that the only idea that the  labour party have  no that was that that's one that would  have the most direct most significant  impact and would be part of an emergency  budget but i also talked about cutting  business rates for small businesses as  well that would help the high streets  going to and help with jobs as well you  know we need a full emergency budget  because this is an emergency situation  this is pressures on on living that  frankly have not been seen in my  lifetime and what we've got at the  moment isn't enough so what you know  we're calling for that emergency budget  so we can take significant action and to  make life easier for people because  they're really struggling at the moment  uh mr norris did you know budget will be  coming in a few months time i mean the  argument would be that if you do an  emergency budget now and you make uh  changes to how the country's finances  look you'll have to do it again in the  autumn because these issues that we're  facing are not going away  yeah well i think this is going to need  you know sustained action i mean the the  the answer's kind of in the question  there we just got to ask people ask our  neighbours you know ask my constituents  can you wait a few more months for  action the message i'm getting back very  clearly is that they cannot wait so  that's why i think we have to act now  rather than kind of hoping we can drift  to to the autumn because i think that  would be really